    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d205">

                <pb facs="0245" n="1079" xml:id="pg1079"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/10787</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Sharp</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-16T18:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 16, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received November 17, 10.17
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5873. War Trade Board [from McFadden]:</p>
                <p>No. 604. Referring to Department’s 5873 of October 11, your No. 366. We are
                    advised by French Ministry of Blockade that they have invited Japanese delegate
                    to participate at Inter-Allied Blacklisting Committees and Enemy Trade License
                    Conference, but that no definite answer has been given, though a representation
                    of Japanese Embassy here has had informal discussion with Blockade on question.
                    We will keep you advised. McFadden.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sharp</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
